# PHP standards

When writing or editing PHP in this project, follow these standards.

---

## 1. PHP 8 constructor property promotion

**Prefer PHP 8 constructor property promotion** over the traditional style (separate property declarations and assignment in `__construct()`).

- **SHOULD** use promoted properties when a constructor only assigns parameters to same-named properties.
- **SHOULD** suggest refactoring existing PHP 7-style constructors to promoted properties when touching that code, when the body is only dependency/property assignment.
- Use **promoted properties** (visibility + type in constructor parameters).
- Add **`readonly`** when dependencies are never reassigned (PHP 8.1+).
- Keep a **trailing comma** in the constructor parameter list.
- If the constructor has validation, event dispatch, or other logic beyond assignment, keep that in the body; only simple assignments can be replaced by promotion.

### Avoid (PHP 7 style when only assigning)

```php
class OrderProcessor
{
    private LoggerInterface $logger;
    private ConfigInterface $config;

    public function __construct(
        LoggerInterface $logger,
        ConfigInterface $config
    ) {
        $this->logger = $logger;
        $this->config = $config;
    }
}
```

### Prefer (PHP 8 style)

```php
class OrderProcessor
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly LoggerInterface $logger,
        private readonly ConfigInterface $config,
    ) {}
}
```

